-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the place read by a good point, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Three function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated by the image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field under coefficientwise extension of scalars; `fieldBar q M'`, the analogous base change of the function field of $X_{H}$ at level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^{2}M')^{\times}\to(\mathbb Z/q)^{\times}$, that is the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; and the characteristic-$q$ fields `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` and `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over the residue field of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` is given, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, the set of $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion affine point. The hypothesis `hle` records the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   The reduction data consist of: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the characteristic-$q$ field with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places, compatibility with $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ on constants, the scaling property `exists_smul_mem`, preservation of degrees and of orders via `mapDomain_placeMap`; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which says that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; an index $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ ([`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21)); and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$.
--
--   The Igusa group of hypotheses: `hIg_inf` identifies $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ (at `lineInfty q`) as the Gauss ring, namely $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot y = x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$; `hIg` says every line $\ell$ is of the form $\mathrm{red}_q(\gamma)\cdot\infty$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pull-back of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the pull-backs along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   The supersingular group: `hSS_A` says that for each $s\in W$ and $x\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ iff $x\in A$; `hSS_over` says that for $s\in W$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ which has no pole where the $q$-expansion $j_q$ has none (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb` implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pull-back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all $\zeta'$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$. Furthermore $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring with surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants and satisfying `exists_smul_mem`), with `hR`: $R.\mathrm{integers} = O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$, and `hR₀O`: $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ iff the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   The arithmetic data: an element $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}\cap A$ with $\pi^{q^{2}-1}=q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the pull-back `A.comap`) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`); a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^{2}-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; finally an intermediate field $K_1$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$, finite over $k_0$, and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ with $A_1 = A\cap K_1$ (`hA₁`), which is a discrete valuation ring and henselian.
--
--   With `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all indices $\zeta'$ and all $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum inside `fieldBar q M'` of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_1$. The assertion is further made for every $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map agrees on $A_1$ with the inclusion $K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`, for every $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by `coeffEmb` applied to `jq`, with $j_1\ne 0$, and for every finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over `ResidueField A` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to that field such that (a) for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue equals $j$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and (b) a place $Q$ lies in $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ precisely when there is $s\in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ iff $j(g)$ in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g$.
--
--   The model in question is $\mathfrak X_1 =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`, the pushout glueing $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A₁ T₁ j₁` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}=\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf A₁ T₁ j₁` (integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$. Five predicates are introduced. For a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and $f\in T_1$: `InStalk x f` holds when for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$-image $x$ there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h\notin y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ and $f\,h=g$ in $T_1$, and the same with $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ and `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the extra requirement $g\in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ in both charts. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` holds when $P$ is rational and every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and satisfies: the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ iff `InMax x f`. The predicate `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$, every $b$ in `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a nonunit of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; the same for $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ and `chartAlgInf`; and for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ (of `jChartFin`) does not lie in `ssJSet q Ω`. The predicate `Reads x Q`, for $Q$ a place of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over `ResidueField A`, holds when every $f$ with `InStalk x f` has its image in `fieldBar q M'` inside $R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that residue is a nonunit of the valuation subring of $Q$ exactly when `InMax x f`. Finally `OffBranch x` holds when for every line $\ell\ne\infty$ and every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$ there is $b$ in `chartAlgFin` whose image is a nonunit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ with $b\notin y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and likewise for $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ and `chartAlgInf`.
--
--   The conclusion is a single statement: for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ with `GoodPt x`, and all places $Q$ and $Q'$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` over `ResidueField A`, if `Reads x Q` and `Reads x Q'` then $Q = Q'$. The predicates `Centred` and `OffBranch` are introduced as abbreviations and do not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case of the uniqueness half of the reading dictionary between closed points of the two-chart integral model of the level field and places of the reduced Igusa function field: a good point of the special fibre, lying on the $\infty$-branch and away from supersingular $j$-invariants, reads at most one place. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel_of_eq_three) in the construction of the semistable covering of the modular curve at level $q^2M'$.
